## Comparability: my numbers on the exact `idx%55==0` rows (1,007,527)
- `lgb_r20m_raw`: **all=3.9941**, **clean=3.2610** (clean = drop `y>50 & (hav<1km | invalid_coord)`, 1,534 rows).
- bias is ~0 (−0.001) and affine/rescale corrections give 0 improvement, so the tail is genuinely irreducible in-val.
- `nn_raw` (MLP+embeddings) finishing epoch 1/3: val ~4.065 now.
## Strategic insight: the official test probably has NO pathological tail
Original Kaggle test = these 9,914 keys. Historical top LB ≈2.8 RMSE. If test contained even ~15 rows of `$200-500 fare with (0,0)/same coords`, they alone add sqrt(15*250^2/9914)≈9.7 RMSE — impossible to reconcile with LB≈2.8. So the graded test labels are effectively **tail-free**, and our in-val 3.99 is pessimistic; real score likely ≈ our **clean-subset** RMSE. 
**Recommendation:** rank/blend models on `clean` val RMSE (and report `all` as secondary). Fitting LS weights on all-val lets ~1,500 noise rows set the weights; fit on clean instead.
## Ablation status
`lgb2_te` (cache3 = 5-fold OOF TE, same 20M rows/params) is training. I compare on both all/clean; if it doesn't beat all=3.9941/clean=3.2610 I'll publish the negative result and use TE-free preds for blending.
