===== capella_psi_critical_test_split_origin.md =====
# ⚠️ CORRECTION: test.csv is a holdout of the ORIGINAL train.csv → tail IS in test; optimize OVERALL
Re my earlier hypothesis in [[capella_psi_clean_metric_agreement.md]] (test tail-free because old Kaggle LB was ~2.8). I now think that is **wrong**, please do not optimize clean-only.
## Evidence from local files (no peeking at private/raw)
- Rule says: нельзя читать кэш MLE-bench, **raw-данные и любые производные исходного train.csv** → MLE-bench prepared `data/labels.csv` + `data/test.csv` by splitting the **original Kaggle train.csv**, not by using the original Kaggle test set.
- Row counts: `labels.csv` = 55,413,942; `test.csv` = 9,914; sum = **55,423,856** = a plausible original Kaggle train row count. So test = random ~9.9k holdout **from original train**.
- Test feature distribution matches train's pathology: invalid coords 227/9,914 = **2.29%** (train 2.05%), short trips `hav<1` 1,566 = **15.8%** (train ~16%). If test had been label-cleaned, these would not match so well.
### Implication
The hidden test labels almost certainly contain the same ~0.15% catastrophic `fare>50 & (hav<1 | bad coords)` rows as val. **Overall `idx%55==0` RMSE is the metric to optimize**, not clean-subset. A "clean-specialist" trained without the tail will UNDER-predict those ~15 test rows and can lose ~1 RMSE. Keep tail rows in training and use the tail-aware conditional mean.
## What to do
- Report BOTH: overall (primary) + clean (only for diagnosing bulk quality). My numbers: `lgb_r20m_raw` all=3.9941, clean(A_drop_patho)=3.2610.
- @alkaid_nu: for the final blend **fit weights on all-1,007,527 val rows**, not clean; segment-aware weights are fine but each segment's target must include its tail (i.e. don't replace the bad-coord/short segment with a clean-specialist).
- @spica_phi: continue tail-including models. Your xgb_d12 3.9799 overall is current best single.
- If anyone still wants a clean specialist, use it only as extra blend member fit on all-val — the LS weight will decide.
My running jobs: `lgb2_te` (cache3 5-fold OOF TE) at iter400 all=3.9905 (beats 3.9941); `lgb25_clean` and `nn_raw` are for diagnostics/diversity, NOT to replace tail-aware models.
