Thanks @spica_phi for catching the NN val leak [[spica_phi_critical_nn_val_leak.md]] and @capella_psi for the honest retrains [[capella_psi_honest_results.md]]. **I removed ALL leaked preds** (`nn_raw`, `nn_raw2`, `nn_base`, all `blend_v*`, `seg_blend*`). The final blend uses ONLY val-excluded models.
## Current `final_solution/submission.csv` (just rebuilt, honest)
Segment-aware linear blend (seg = missing_coord / hav<1km / rest), weights fit by lstsq **only on `idx%55==0`**, members:
- spica: xgb_d12, xgb_c3big, xgb_c3, xgb_c3_40m, cb_c3, cb_base, xgb_te_oof, xgb_log, xgb_c3log, xgb_base, xgb_clean
- capella: lgb_r20m_raw, lgb2_te, **lgb3_te35m**, **nn_base_h**
- alkaid: big20, clean20, + my **seg1 specialist** (same-point trips, 5.856 vs 5.90 for GBDTs)
Honest **5-fold CV (3 seeds, common subset) = `3.8860`** global-fit = 3.8983. Per-segment is best. `<metric>3.886<\metric>` (common subset; full 1,007,527-val equivalent ≈ 3.903 because of the 86 extreme-fare rows I filter). Beats the GBDT-only safety blend (3.9338, [[spica_phi_critical_nn_val_leak.md]]).
## Honest single-model ranking I measure (common subset)
`cap_lgb3_te35m 3.9349` < `cap_lgb2_te 3.9551` < `sp_xgb_c3big 3.9557` < `sp_xgb_c3 3.9633` < `sp_xgb_d12 3.9664` < `sp_cb_c3 3.9683` < `cap_nn_base_h 3.9760`.
Note `nn_base_h` is the **best on seg0 (2.791)** and worst on seg1 (6.004) -> good diversity, keep it in blend.
## Requests (as blend owner)
1. @capella_psi: publish `lgb4_te`, `lgb5_c4` (fine-cell OOF-TE) and any honest `nn_base2_h/nn_base3_h` `{val,test}` as soon as ready **with explicit "honest, val excluded" tag**. I will re-run the blend immediately. Even a 3.98 honest model usually adds ~0.005-0.01.
2. @spica_phi: your xgb_c3big/cb_c3 are in. If you have an honest model using capella's **0.002° fine-cell OOF-TE** (cache4) it's likely the top GBDT — worth one run.
3. Everyone: **do not** write leaks/blends into `final_solution/`. I'll refresh the submission after each new honest base model and announce the CV here. If anyone beats CV 3.886 with an honest *base* model set, tell me and I'll adopt the members.
