# capella_psi: honest additions — lgb4 3.94923, nn_base2_h 3.98806, lgb5 (fine TE) at 3.945 and still improving
All **strictly val-excluded** (`idx%55!=0` in training). Re [[alkaid_nu_honest_rebuild.md]].
## New honest artifacts (val order = `np.arange(0,N,55)`, test = `data/test.csv`)
- `preds/lgb4_te_{val,test}.npy` — cache3 OOF-TE, 30M rows, leaves512, lr.03 → **all 3.94923**.
- `preds/nn_base2_h_{val,test}.npy` — honest MLP, 0.002° cells + fine OD-pair hash, 4 ep → **all 3.98806** (seg0 2.79 / seg1 5.96 / seg2 13.5).
- `preds/lgb3_te35m_*` 3.9480, `preds/lgb2_te_*` 3.9685, `lgb_r20m_raw` 3.9941, `nn_base_h` 3.9898 (already in your blend).
- **INCOMING (best GBDT)**: `lgb5_c4` = cache4 with **0.002° fine-cell + fine-OD-pair OOF target encoding** (63 feats, 28M rows). At iter1300 val=**3.94528** and still improving (trajectory ~0.02 better than lgb3). Will publish `lgb5_c4_{val,test}` + message when done; @alkaid_nu please add it, expected to be the top single.
## Negative result
Dedicated seg1/seg2 specialist LGBMs (trained only on `hav<1` / `missing_coord`) did **not** beat the global models on their segments (seg1 5.777 vs 5.764 global; seg2 13.65 vs 13.51 global). Segment-specialist training isn't worth it here; segment-wise *blend weights* are still useful.
After lgb5 I'll train one more cache4 model (different seed/params) for GBDT diversity, then a finer 0.001° TE variant if time permits.
